-- The minimum amount annexes ד–ו give, for the post, the classes and the
-- seniority in management: the input §16's `the minimum amount` takes (`annex ד's amount for the post, classes and seniority`); NOTHING
-- where the table leaves the cell empty.
GIVEN `the cells` IS A LIST OF `managers' minimum of 23.9.2024`
      classes IS A NUMBER
      seniority IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the managers' minimum of 23.9.2024 in` `the cells` classes seniority IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `its classes, 23.9.2024` EQUALS classes AND c's `its seniority in management, 23.9.2024` EQUALS seniority) `the cells`
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (c's `its amount, 23.9.2024`)
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING

#ASSERT `the managers' minimum of 23.9.2024 in` `the minimum amounts of annex ד' of 23.9.2024` 32 16 EQUALS JUST 30000
#ASSERT `the managers' minimum of 23.9.2024 in` `the minimum amounts of annex ד' of 23.9.2024` 32 1 EQUALS JUST 24000
#ASSERT `the managers' minimum of 23.9.2024 in` `the minimum amounts of annex ד' of 23.9.2024` 1 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the managers' minimum of 23.9.2024 in` `the minimum amounts of annex ה' of 23.9.2024` 32 1 EQUALS JUST 19200
#ASSERT `the managers' minimum of 23.9.2024 in` `the minimum amounts of annex ו' of 23.9.2024` 32 2 EQUALS JUST 20910


§§ `Worked examples`

-- Examples and checks.

`a teacher in the reform` MEANS
    `upper-division employee` WITH
        `represented by the teachers' organization` IS TRUE
        `covered by the Oz LaTmura agreement`        IS TRUE
        `employed under Oz LaTmura terms`            IS TRUE
        `is a principal`                             IS FALSE

`a teacher outside the reform` MEANS
    `upper-division employee` WITH
        `represented by the teachers' organization` IS TRUE
        `covered by the Oz LaTmura agreement`        IS TRUE
        `employed under Oz LaTmura terms`            IS FALSE
        `is a principal`                             IS FALSE

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, s IS A `grant month status`, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `grant month`
DECIDE `months of` n s p IS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE `grant month` s p FOLLOWED BY `months of` (n MINUS 1) s p

#ASSERT `the one-time grant` `a teacher in the reform` (`months of` 12 `worked` 1) EQUALS 9600
#ASSERT `the one-time grant` `a teacher outside the reform` (`months of` 12 `worked` 1) EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT `the one-time grant` `a teacher in the reform` (`months of` 12 `worked` 1.1) EQUALS 10560
#ASSERT `the one-time grant` `a teacher in the reform` (append (`months of` 6 `worked` 1) (`months of` 6 `unpaid leave or sabbatical` 1)) EQUALS 4800

-- 7(ב)'s table: each total is the sum of its pulses.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD sum (LIST r's `pulse 1`, r's `pulse 2`, r's `pulse 3`, r's `pulse 4`) EQUALS r's `pulse total`) `the table of the Oz 2023 shekel supplement`
#ASSERT `the Oz 2023 shekel supplement` `a teacher in the reform` 0.5 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2026) EQUALS 895.25
#ASSERT `the Oz 2023 shekel supplement` `a teacher outside the reform` 1 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2026) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the 2023 shekel supplement` `a teacher outside the reform` 1.2 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) EQUALS 600

-- 8: the 38 hours are 25 + 3 + 10, and the 10 are 2 + 2 + 1 + 5.
#ASSERT `frontal hours` PLUS `individual hours` PLUS `teaching-support hours` EQUALS `the position base in weekly hours`
#ASSERT sum `support hours by activity` EQUALS `teaching-support hours`

#ASSERT `the homeroom or grade-coordinator reward` `homeroom teacher` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024) 800 700 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the role reward rate` `ICT and technology coordinator` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2025) (6%) EQUALS 8%
#ASSERT `the special-education rate from 1.9.2024` (14%) TRUE EQUALS 17%

-- 14(ה)'s own example: four units, 800 a month.
#ASSERT `the school role reward` `a teacher in the reform` FALSE 4 0.5 1 EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `the school role reward` `a teacher in the reform` FALSE 4 0.3 1 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the school role reward` `a teacher outside the reform` FALSE 4 1 1 EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `the managerial supplement` `vice-principal` TRUE `first degree` 12 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2025) 20000 (LIST `manager's component` `ordinary component` 17000, `manager's component` `homeroom reward` 1000, `manager's component` `overtime or single hours` 1000) EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `the managerial supplement` `principal` TRUE `first degree` 12 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2025) 20000 (LIST `manager's component` `ordinary component` 17000, `manager's component` `overtime or single hours` 1000) EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `the technological final-exam reward` 4 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the technological final-exam reward` 6 EQUALS 3.5
#ASSERT `the Israeli Journey grant` 5 EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `the special-contract ceiling` 10 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the special-contract ceiling` 50 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the flexible reward paid this year` 2 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0.7
#ASSERT `the hours skipped are allowed` 6 2 4
#ASSERT NOT `the hours skipped are allowed` 5 2 4

-- The first academisation example follows the rule.
#ASSERT `the academisation share` 1.05 1 2 EQUALS 0.525
#ASSERT `the academisation share` (1.4%) 1 2 EQUALS 0.7%
#TRACE `the grant is paid` 9600 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the one-time grant` 9600 AT 2
#TRACE `the grant is paid` 9600 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the one-time grant` 6000 AT 2
#TRACE `the retirement grant is paid` 120000 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the retirement grant` 120000 AT 25
